spes: IPA draft review fixes (0213).

Adversarial review of 0210 against Linux v6.12 drivers/net/ipa and the phone's own downstream kernel (drivers/platform/msm/ipa,
gsi; CONFIG_ARCH_KHAJE): GPI channel scratch: max_outstanding_tre goes to SCRATCH_2[31:16] and outstanding_threshold to
SCRATCH_3[31:16], SCRATCH_0/1 reserved (Linux gsi_channel_program, msm_gsi.h); command channel 64 TREs (tre_count >= 2*tlv-1, power
of two, gsi_channel_data_valid); static trace -> ipa_trace (bsd/sys/trace.h macro). Confirmed: IPA base 0x5840000 and SRAM +0x7000
(ipahal_get_reg_base, ipa3_init_sram), RPM_SMD_IPA_CLK 0x617069, all v4.2/GSI register fields, endpoint/channel map. Open: clock
only in the active set, 100 MHz vs downstream 125, no msm-bus votes (all-6 hung later in boot with the full IPA set up).

